840 by the Portuguese colonial administration. Strategically located near the Namib Desert, it plays a significant role in the history of colonial Angola and the broader regional dynamics in Southern Africa. The city was known as Namibe from 1985 to 2016, reflecting its evolving identity within the context of Angolan independence and post-colonial governance. It is notable for its cool dry climate, characterized by desert vegetation, which distinguishes it from much of the humid tropics of Angola.

